  "id": "family-intervention",
  "term": "family intervention",
  "definition": "Family intervention is a psychosocial approach for schizophrenia that works with the person and their family or carers to help reduce relapse and lessen illness burden. It may be adapted to fit cultural beliefs and local circumstances so it can be delivered effectively in different settings.",
